<%#
  Why a step refused to advance.

  The three validations that can refuse a step used to write their messages
  into the path_entry hash, which is discarded on exactly that branch — so the
  markup for showing them was never reached and never written. The messages
  now arrive on the outcome and land here.

  locals: errors — array of strings, empty when the step was not refused
%>
<% if errors.any? %>
  <div class="form-error" id="runner-step-errors" role="alert">
    <% if errors.one? %>
      <%= errors.first %>
    <% else %>
      <ul class="form-error__list">
        <% errors.each do |message| %>
          <li><%= message %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
